<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ali Nasir Muhammad</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">b. 1939</span> · Also known as Ali Nasser Mohammed</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ali Nasir Muhammad is a Yemeni politician who was prime minister of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-yemen">South Yemen</a> from 1971 to 1985 and head of state and general secretary of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yemeni-socialist-party">Yemeni Socialist Party</a> from 1980 to 1986. He followed a more pragmatic course, improving relations with Saudi <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabia">Arabia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oman">Oman</a> and the West. In January 1986 his attempt to eliminate his rivals set off a brief civil war, which he lost, and he fled to North <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yemen">Yemen</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ali-nasir-muhammad.jpg" alt="Ali Nasir Muhammad" width="320" height="357" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ali_Nasser_Muhammad_USSR_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
